description:
Found s504 by s501t: t/op/magic.t row #66 (`print $? & 0xFF ? "ok $tn[4]" : "not ok $tn[4]"` after a child that kills itself with SIGINT) became a NUMBERED `not ok` once `tie my @tn` worked (#155); under main the same line printed an unnumbered `not ok` (the untied @tn gave no number).  PRE-EXISTING: same answer on main b7ec0093.

Reproducer (perl prints `status=2 sig=2`; PCL prints `status=512 sig=0`, on main and on the s501t tree):
    open(CMDPIPE, "|-", "perl") or die;
    print CMDPIPE '$SIG{INT} = "DEFAULT"; kill "INT", $$; sleep 1;';
    close CMDPIPE;
    printf "status=%d sig=%d\n", $?, $? & 0xFF;

`system(LIST)` is right (s501t probe: a PCL or perl child killed by SIGINT gives sig=2), so it is the piped-open CLOSE path that converts the wait status -- most likely it waits through a shell or reads the process's exit CODE (128+N folded, or SBCL's process-exit-code) instead of the raw wait status.  Layer: runtime (close of a pipe handle); sibling of #2101 (backticks $?), #1770.  Guard: a Pl/t row with the reproducer above.
